# AudioSR low-VRAM / Web UI fork — provenance notice

This repository is a MODIFIED VERSION of AudioSR:

    Upstream : https://github.com/haoheliu/versatile_audio_super_resolution
    Paper    : Liu, Chen, Tian, Wang, Plumbley — "AudioSR: Versatile Audio
               Super-Resolution at Scale", ICASSP 2024 (arXiv:2309.07314)
    License  : MIT — the upstream LICENSE file is kept unchanged in ./LICENSE

All copyright of the upstream code, the model architecture, the training /
inference algorithm (the `audiosr/` package) and the bundled example assets
belongs to the original authors. No upstream file was altered by this fork.

Additions made in this repository (all additive, Windows-oriented tooling):

    run_lowvram.py             low-VRAM inference wrapper: fp16 UNet on the
                               GPU, VAE/vocoder on the CPU, SDPA attention,
                               chunked long-audio inference, true-stereo
                               per-channel processing, resampling and
                               ffmpeg-based output conversion
    webui_server.py            local web UI (standard library only, optional
                               LAN access, model kept resident in memory)
    双击启动网页界面.cmd         one-click local Web UI launcher
    双击启动局域网网页界面.cmd   one-click LAN Web UI launcher (0.0.0.0)
    双击选择音频处理.cmd +
    pick_and_run.py            double-click "pick a file, process it" helper
    run_audiosr.cmd            command-line launcher
    test_formats.py,
    test_192k.py,
    test_outsr.py,
    check_output.py            self-check / validation scripts
    README.md                  Chinese documentation for the additions (also
                               rendered on the repository front page)
    README_EN.md               the upstream English README (kept unchanged,
                               plus the fork notice at the top)

Not included in this repository: the Python virtual environment (`.venv/`),
the model weights (`pytorch_model.bin`), generated audio (`output*/`) and the
Web UI upload cache (`webui_uploads/`) — all excluded via `.gitignore`.

Two upstream files were modified on purpose:

    requirements.txt           the `git+https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers.git`
                               line is commented out. Nothing in this repository
                               imports `diffusers` (verified), and cloning from
                               GitHub inside pip frequently fails in CN networks
                               ("Recv failure: Connection was reset"), which
                               aborted the whole install. Re-enable it if you
                               actually need diffusers.

    audiosr/clap/training/data.py
                               `RobertaTokenizer.from_pretrained("roberta-base")`
                               used to run at import time, which pulled ~500 MB
                               from the Hub (or broke offline starts) even though
                               the AudioSR inference path never uses the CLAP text
                               tokenizer. It is now loaded lazily on first use.

Nothing else inside `audiosr/` (model architecture, training and inference
code) was changed.

If this fork is useful to you, please star and cite the upstream project.
